    "family_reading": {
        "text": "ByteDance Seed's Seed line offers six API-only versions, all with reasoning support and none with open weights, so self-hosting is not an option. Every version carries a 262144 token context window, though maximum output varies widely, from 32768 tokens on the two Seed 1.6 releases up to 235929 on Seed 2.1 Turbo. Inputs can include image, text and video, with text-only output. Pricing spans a broad range, from $0.08 per million input and $0.3 output on Seed 1.6 Flash to $0.5 input and $2.5 output on Seed 2.1 Turbo, with Seed-2.0-Code at $3 output. The facts suggest the family suits long-context multimodal work and reasoning tasks where an API is acceptable, with cheaper tiers for high-volume use. Limits include the absence of open weights, the cost of the larger output tiers, and the smaller output ceiling on the 1.6 versions.",
